        <dc:title>Designing a Reinforcement Learning Approach for the NFV Orchestration System with Energy Saving Optimization</dc:title>
        <dcterms:abstract>With the development of 5G mobile system, the concept of Network Functions Virtualization (NFV) is gaining importance. In the 3GPP standards organization's fifth generation mobile technology network specification, network slicing composed of virtualized network functions (VNFs) is proposed as one of the key technologies for 5G. In addition, for telecom operators, they are more concerned about how to deploy VNFs composed of network slices to optimize resource utilization and reduce resource wastage, in order to achieve operational cost savings. This study designs an energy-saving scheduler module for Kubernetes-based NFV orchestration system. And reinforcement learning approach is applied to make placement decisions for VNFs in network slices, scheduling to place the required VNFs in the least number of compute nodes without affecting deployed services. Further, the scheduler can leave idle compute nodes in shutdown or standby state to reduce resource usage and achieve energy efficiency.</dcterms:abstract>
        <dc:date>2022</dc:date>
