        <link:link rdf:resource="#item_261"/>
        <link:link rdf:resource="#item_262"/>
        <dc:title>Assigning Pods to Nodes</dc:title>
        <dcterms:abstract>You can constrain a Pod so that it is restricted to run on particular node(s), or to prefer to run on particular nodes. There are several ways to do this and the recommended approaches all use label selectors to facilitate the selection. Often, you do not need to set any such constraints; the scheduler will automatically do a reasonable placement (for example, spreading your Pods across nodes so as not place Pods on a node with insufficient free resources).</dcterms:abstract>
        <dc:identifier>
            <dcterms:URI>
                <rdf:value>https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/scheduling-eviction/assign-pod-node/</rdf:value>
            </dcterms:URI>
