        <link:link rdf:resource="#item_264"/>
        <dc:title>Kubernetes Scheduler</dc:title>
        <dcterms:abstract>In Kubernetes, scheduling refers to making sure that Pods are matched to Nodes so that Kubelet can run them.
Scheduling overview A scheduler watches for newly created Pods that have no Node assigned. For every Pod that the scheduler discovers, the scheduler becomes responsible for finding the best Node for that Pod to run on. The scheduler reaches this placement decision taking into account the scheduling principles described below.</dcterms:abstract>
        <dc:identifier>
            <dcterms:URI>
                <rdf:value>https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/scheduling-eviction/kube-scheduler/</rdf:value>
            </dcterms:URI>
        </dc:identifier>
